  "limitations": [
    "Trivial chooses the first non-pass non-mana priority action; attacks using AllAttackersStrategy; takes the first option elsewhere. No scoring, observation, LLM or search.",
    "It keeps its opening hand, normally never blocks, and tries each priority ability once per turn/phase.",
    "Different agents produce different trajectories and consume different amounts of lazy option generation. A whole-game difference is not a direct measurement of scoring overhead.",
    "Timing batches disable decision telemetry and match logs; diagnostic batches are separate instrumented runs.",
    "Active generation times top-level next() intervals, including nested expansion once, excluding consumer time. Other decision time includes discovery outside streams, policy, validation and instrumentation. Precomputed choices are generated before decide() and are not part of its generation interval.",
    "Outside-decisions time includes engine execution, setup and observer/orchestration overhead. This is a minimal-policy workload, not a policy-free replay of an identical game.",
    "Controller decision counts differ in coverage: Trivial counts every request, including setup; older agents count their recorded decisions. Use diagnostic timed_decisions for complete request counts."
